# Test: an operator who writes plaintext-password in a config FILE can log in.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-netlab-integration AC-1 and AC-3 -- a config loaded at daemon
#            start hashes the plaintext-password sibling into the canonical
#            password leaf, so LocalAuthenticator accepts the login, and the
#            daemon warns once that the plaintext is still in the file.
# PREVENTS:  the defect recorded in plan/journal/silent-fall-through.md on
#            2026-08-14. ApplyPasswordHashing (internal/component/config/
#            password_hash.go) had callers only on the editor commit path, so a
#            config FILE carrying plaintext-password loaded with an empty
#            canonical leaf. CheckPassword (internal/component/authz/auth.go)
#            then refused every login for that user, `ze config validate` called
#            the file valid, and nothing anywhere said why.
#
# This is the user-visible half of the fix. The unit tests in
# internal/component/config/loader_test.go prove the transform on the tree; only
# a running daemon proves the credential the transform produced authenticates.
#
# DISCRIMINATOR: revert the ApplyPasswordHashing call in LoadConfig and seq 1
# fails at the login step with "SSH auth failure", because the canonical leaf is
# empty and CheckPassword refuses an empty hash. Nothing else in the file
# changes: the daemon still starts and still answers on the SSH port.
#
# The config dir is emptied for the CLI (as in cli-credential-resolution.ci,
# whose shape this test follows) so no credential store can supply a login: the
# only credential in play is the one the config file declared.
#
# SUITE: this lives in test/plugin because the compiled fixture starts a daemon
# and then logs in through the plugin runner's bare-name binary shims.

tmpfs=plaintext-at-boot.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 65533
			}
		}
	}
}

system {
	authentication {
		user lab {
			plaintext-password "labsecret"
		}
	}
}

environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port 0;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/config-plaintext-password-at-boot:timeout=25s
expect=exit:code=0
